# Polish pass

- Stack: Next.js 15 App Router (do not downgrade), TypeScript, Tailwind. Server components by default, "use client" only where interactivity needs it.
- Never change, move or restyle these live routes or their data/state: /champions-draft, /rugby-draft, /pub-quiz, /games/longest-word, /draft, /wardrobe-ai, and anything under them. Linking to them is fine. If you edit a shared component, check every file that imports it.
- /stout-finder redirects to stoutfinder.com. Leave that redirect in place.
- Keep every existing route working. Change nav labels, not URLs.
- Anything under /hire stays unless a prompt says otherwise. The hire-meter finale card, the Rudi modal, and the FELINE_DISTRACTION_DETECTED card are intentional. Never remove or alter them.
- Contact forms stay on Formspree. Don't change action, method or field names.
- Don't weaken Supabase RLS. No secrets or service keys in client code.
- Design: base #0A0A0F, amber #F59E0B as the only strong accent. DM Serif Display for headings, Geist for body, Geist Mono for labels. No new fonts or colour tokens. Opacity tints of existing colours are fine.
- No new npm dependencies unless the task explicitly allows one.
- Copy: no em dashes or en dashes, use plain hyphens. No filler. Banned: passionate, journey, seamless, leverage, crafting digital experiences, "I'd love to", "reaching out", circling back, synergy. Plain, dry NI English.
- Never invent metrics, client results, user counts or testimonials. Keep client status labels exactly as currently written.
- Assisi rebrand: built, awaiting their sign-off. Never say they have adopted it.
- ShelterLink: ready for live use. Never say Assisi is using it.
- RV's Cold Brew: Square is linked, a few details left. Never claim working online ordering or payments.
- All animation respects prefers-reduced-motion.
- After every task: npm run build and npm run lint pass, then commit with a clear message.
